From cd91fe4415e303f771be466caa2f4c96960b1b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "SN Fast Sync (local)" <snfast@localhost.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:36:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build(mobile): open the push websocket in the mobile app (it
 never opened one)

The page that the mobile apps load (packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html) sets window.websocketUrl to an
empty string, while the web app's own page uses wss://sockets.standardnotes.com. With an empty URL
WebSocketsService.startWebSocketConnection() returns "WebSocket URL is not set" and the Android and iOS apps never
open a push channel: they only poll every 30 s (the websocket-closed branch of autoSync) and on window focus. Use the
same URL as the web app, so the server's "items changed" notification reaches the phone while the app is open and the
fast-sync patches can act on it. Only used for the hosted server; a custom sync server still brings its own URL
(Advanced options), which is stored and wins.
---
 packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html b/packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html
index 7cf4b31..1ade574 100644
--- a/packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html
+++ b/packages/mobile/html/Web.bundle/src/index.html
@@ -13,3 +13,3 @@
         window.enabledUnfinishedFeatures = "" === 'true';
-        window.websocketUrl = "";
+        window.websocketUrl = "wss://sockets.standardnotes.com";
         window.purchaseUrl = "https://standardnotes.com/purchase";
-- 
